          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "せんたく — sentaku — \"washing clothes; the washing\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "せんたくは あにの しごとです。 — sentaku wa ani no shigoto desu — \"The washing is my elder brother's job.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "せんたく (sentaku) is Sino-Japanese (kango): two Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese. They are sen, \"wash\", whose sound matches the rhyme book's senX although it gives \"wash\" under sejX, and taku, \"rinse\" (Middle Chinese draewk) (KANJIDIC2; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for everyday life at A2."
